.TH "DOT\-ORPHAN" "1" "August 2026" ""
.SH "NAME"
\fBdot\-orphan\fR \- Unlink managed dotfile(s) and remove them from the repository
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
\fBdot orphan\fR [\-h] \fIfile\fR\|\.\|\.\|\.
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Orphan one or more local dotfiles from the user's home folder into the dotfiles repository by:
.IP "1." 4
Unlinking it
.IP "2." 4
Copying the real file to the user's $HOME
.IP "3." 4
Removing the real file from the dotfiles repository and managed\.files\. If you wish to keep the file in the repo, use \fB\-k\fR\.
.IP "" 0
.P
This converts a once managed dotfile to a local\-only dotfile\.
.P
To simply mark a dotfile already present in the dotfiles repository as managed, see dot\-manage(1)\.
.P
Part of dot(1)\.
.SH "OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-h\fR
Show command help\.
.TP
\fB\-k\fR, \fB\-\-keep\fR
Do not remove the file from the dotfile repository after orphaning
.TP
\fIfile\fR
One or more managed files\. Paths are relative to the dotfile repo\.

